# Generated artifacts — collapsed in GitHub diffs and excluded from language
# stats. They are still tracked and required on disk; this only stops them from
# adding review noise. Reviewers can always expand them manually.

# Drizzle migration metadata: snapshots are the state drizzle-kit diffs against
# to generate the next migration, and _journal.json is its ordering ledger.
# Both are machine-generated by `pnpm db:generate`. The *.sql migration files
# are intentionally NOT marked generated — that DDL runs against production and
# must be reviewed.
#
# Matched directory-agnostically so any package's drizzle meta is covered
# (libs/database/drizzle/meta, libs/agent-daemon-state/drizzle-pg/meta,
# libs/agent-daemon-state/drizzle-sqlite/meta, and any future ones).
**/meta/*_snapshot.json linguist-generated=true
**/meta/_journal.json linguist-generated=true

# OpenAPI-generated clients. Keep the checked-in TypeScript and Go clients
# available to consumers while collapsing regeneration noise in GitHub diffs
# and excluding it from repository language statistics.
libs/api-client/src/generated/** linguist-generated=true
libs/signer-api-client/src/generated/** linguist-generated=true
libs/moltnet-api-client/*_gen.go linguist-generated=true

# Vendored third-party skill (impeccable, Apache-2.0). ~2.8MB of generated
# .mjs per provider tree — keep out of language stats and collapse diff noise.
**/skills/impeccable/** linguist-vendored=true

# CodeBoarding owns this versioned architecture baseline. Collapse it in
# GitHub diffs and exclude it from language statistics while keeping the
# hand-maintained ignore configuration reviewable.
.codeboarding/** linguist-generated=true
.codeboarding/.codeboardingignore -linguist-generated
